{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "רוקח", :translit "rokeach", :gloss "compounder"} {:he "ב' מלאים", :translit "bet melaim", :gloss "two times plene"} {:he "מעשה רוקח", :translit "ma'aseh rokeach", :gloss "the compounder's work"} {:he "זבובי מות", :translit "zvovei mavet", :gloss "dead flies"} {:he "שמן רוקח", :translit "shemen rokeach", :gloss "compounder's oil"} {:he "מות גבי רוקח", :translit "mavet gabei rokeach", :gloss "death by compounder"} {:he "ויתן את הקטורת ויכפר על העם", :translit "vayiten et ha-ketoret vayekhaper al ha-am", :gloss "and he placed the incense and made atonement for the people"} {:he "טהור קדש", :translit "tahor kodesh", :gloss "pure, holy"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Word רוקח appears twice plene (with vav) in Scripture: Exodus 30:25 and Ecclesiastes 10:1"}], :frame {:text "Our Rabbis expounded that the people murmured against the incense, saying that by it Nadav and Avihu died (Leviticus 10:2) and by it the assembly of Korah died (Numbers 17:35). The link to רוקח rests on Ecclesiastes 10:1, where רוקח is juxtaposed with מות. Moses countered that the incense does not kill but gives life, as stated in Numbers 17:12, ויתן את הקטורת ויכפר על העם, and as the verse calls it טהור קדש in Exodus 30:35 — rather, the sin is what kills.", :sources ["Leviticus 10:2" "Numbers 17:35" "Ecclesiastes 10:1" "Numbers 17:12" "Exodus 30:35"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Word רוקח appears twice plene (with vav) in Scripture: Exodus 30:25 and Ecclesiastes 10:1", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:20:19.695160142Z", :model "glm-5.2"}